> 
> Just at a guess... Is it possible that you're on a bones level? I
> don't know for certain, but I think when a bones level is restored, it
> is restored exactly as it was when the previous player died. So if
> there was a cockatrice there, it would still be there when you find
> the level.

I think that even on a bones level monsters genocided will stay genocided.
More likely is that you have found a chameleon. Either kill it like it
is, or wait for it to change into a newt or something. Of course, it
might turn into a black dragon first....

> 
> Now a question of my own -- do people really find cockatrices to be
> problem? I've never found them to be worth genociding. I always carry
> around 2 or 3 dead lizards, but I can't remember the last time I
> actually needed to use one. But, I do play a very conservative game,
> and by the time I'm running into cockatrices, they're usually one- or
> two-swing kills. The main danger I find from them is if I'm blinded
> and ungloved, and accidentally feel one.

Never bother myself. Liches etc are much more worthe genociding. Your god
will always help too, long as you don't pray too much. I usually drop
the lizards and rely on divine intervention, but it's pretty rare that
you get stoned once your AC is good enough. (And once you can kill them
in 2 hits.)

> 
> As for genociding, the things I take out are generally nymphs, nurses,
> xans, and umber hulks. And after that I go for cockatrices, but when
> was the last time you ever found more than 4 scrolls of genocide?

None of those things are that bad! Xans are easy, just wear boots. Unber
Hulks are harder, but carry a unicorn horn and they become no more dangerous
than a dragon. Nymphs are easy, hit them with a wand (sleep maybe, or a
ray one) or throw missiles at them. Nurses don't matter much. I usually
don't bother taking my armor off but you just leave them alone. (Or kill
them if you don't mind bad luck. With a blessed luckstone and lots of
sacrifices it rarely matters.)

